! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.73 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.80) --
! SORT THE UNIT COUNT TABLE, then the MULTI UNIT SCAN.
!
! Fifty-six lines, forty-one of which compile.  FOUR boxed headings,
! the most on any page of the ASSIGN program so far:
!
!   lines  4-7   "SORT THE UNIT COUNT TABLE"
!   lines 22-24  "MULTI UNIT SCAN"
!   lines 37-40  "ADVANCE THE UNIT COUNT TABLE FOR ANOTHER CHANNEL"
!   lines 51-53  "ADD TO THE UNIT COUNT IN THE MULTI UNIT TABLE"
!
! >>> LINE 25 IS THE ADDRESS THE BOOT RUN'S TRAIL NOW NAMES. <<<
!
! printed p.72 line 27 is "BB,T MULTI(T IXF),T A9D" -- if the channel
! is a multi-unit channel -- and T A9D is 004275.40, which is this
! page's line 25.  The run walks the channel status table on p.72 and
! leaves it here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A SORT, AND IT IS A BUBBLE SORT <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 8-18 are a two-deep loop over the multi-unit count table:
!
!   T D9A  LX,T IXF,T IXH        the inner index starts at the outer
!          LF(BU,32),0.0(T IXH),32   hold this entry in the accumulator
!   T D9B  KF,T CHCNT(T IXF),40  compare its count with a later one
!          BZAH,T D9C            if ours is not high, leave it
!          LV,T IXG,0.0(T IXF)   otherwise swap: take the later entry
!          ST(BU,32),0.0(T IXF),32    write ours into its slot
!          SV,T IXG,$R           and carry the later one along
!   T D9C  CBH,T IXF,T D9B       count the inner index and repeat
!          ST(BU,32),0.0(T IXH),32    deposit the winner
!          CBH,T IXH,T D9A       count the outer index and repeat
!
! The two CBH rows are what name the two loops apart, and they are
! told apart ONLY by their index fields: line 16 compiles
! 004267.24 C8 (bits 19-22 = 1010 = T IXF) and line 18 compiles
! 004265.04 C8 (bits 19-22 = 0010 = T IXH).  The statement column
! reads F and H at a size where those two glyphs are the hardest
! pair on the page, and the machine code is what settles it --
! see the note on line 2 below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE INDEX FIELD CAUGHT A MISREAD STATEMENT <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 2 read "LVI,T IXF,T CHCUC" at 600 dpi.  Its code is
! 003661.05 01, whose bits 19-22 are 0010 = $2 = T IXH, NOT 1010 =
! $10 = T IXF.  At 1200 dpi the glyph is an H.  Lines 3, 18, 41, 44,
! 45, 46 and 55 all carry T IXH for the same reason, and line 36's
! T IXG (.21, bits 19-22 = 1000) is a third letter in the same
! column.  THE CODE COLUMN IS THE AUTHORITY FOR AN INDEX NAME.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> M+1, AN OPERATION THE ASSEMBLER HAD AND NO PAGE HAD USED <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 55 is "M+1,T CHCNT(T IXH)" -- ADD ONE TO MEMORY -- compiling
! 000000.24 82  004000.22 B0.  Its byte is B0 where p.72 line 26's
! plain "M+" is 90, and the arithmetic is exact: a VFL operation's
! low four bits are the byte's high nibble and its high bits sit in
! bits 22-23 of the second group.  M+1 is operation 43 = 0b101011,
! so the byte is 0xB0 (1011) and bit 22 carries the 32, printing
! ".22" where M+ (operation 9) prints ".20" and * (25) prints ".21".
! Three operations, one byte apart in the printed column, and all
! three now agree with opcodes.VFL_INT_CODES without a change to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> TWO BYTES THE C/ZERO RULE DECIDED, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 33's row prints "004306.C3 C1".  The octal pair cannot hold
! a C (listing_typography.md 13e), so ".C3" is ".03" -- and the row
! is p.72 line 32's twin, "T A9BA LVI,T X1BR,T B9" = 004246.03 01,
! which fixes the byte as 01 as well.  A per-row artifact, 13d.
!
! Line 35's row prints "C04322.74 CO" and line 42's "C04246.34 C2".
! Here the leading C of the LOCATION is a zero both times, but the
! BYTES are real C's: p.72 line 34's "BZRZ,T A10" is 004320.34 C0
! and its line 18's "BRZ,T B9B" is 004261.74 C2.  Same page, same
! two mnemonics, same two bytes.  The octal field and the hex field
! take the C/zero rule in OPPOSITE directions in one row.
!
! TWO LISTING MARKS, the bare "*" after the location that every
! earlier page has carried unexplained: lines 25 and 44.
!
! THE FIRST COUNT HERE WAS WRONG AND THE CROP IS WHY.  "Four marks,
! lines 32, 33, 36 and 54" was read off the right edge of the CODE
! crop -- but 900 dpi x=4200 W=3000 ends at 7200 and the statement
! column starts at 6150, so what bled in was the leading "T" of
! T A9F, T A9FA, T A9G and T C9, which are exactly the four LABELLED
! lines in that range.  A listing mark sits in the LOCATION column,
! and in the location column this page has two.

        SLC, (8)4263.0

! ---- index names, printed p.61 ------------------------------------
TX1BR   SYN, $1
TIXF    SYN, $10
TIXG    SYN, $8
TIXH    SYN, $2
TCTWDX  SYN, $10
! ---- words, printed pp.61-64 --------------------------------------
TLUCT   SYN(BU,18), (8)3273.0
TFCHSC  SYN, (8)3657.0
TRCHSC  SYN, (8)3660.0
TCHCUC  SYN, (8)3661.0
! ---- table offsets, printed pp.62-64 ------------------------------
TUNTBA  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TCHADD  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TCHCNT  SYN(BU,4), 0.20
TCHAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.25
TUNAVL  SYN(BU,1), 0.28
TUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29
TCHOWN  SYN(BU,1), 0.32
TEQUIP  SYN(BU,4), 0.52
TUNITK  SYN(BU,4), 0.59
TUNRES  SYN(BU,1), 0.62
! ---- back, onto printed pp.65 and 72 ------------------------------
TB1F    SYN, (8)3704.0
TB9     SYN, (8)4246.0
! ---- forward, past this page --------------------------------------
TC10    SYN, (8)4322.40
TN      SYN, (8)4422.40

        SLC, (8)4263.0

        CM1111(BU,1), TRCHSC+.24     ! line 1  -SET THE REVERSE SCAN
        LVI, TIXH, TCHCUC            ! line 2
        SX, TIXH, TFCHSC             ! line 3

! ---- SORT THE UNIT COUNT TABLE ------------------------------------
TD9A    LX, TIXF, TIXH               ! line 8
        BXCZ, TD9                    ! line 9
        LF(BU,32), 0.0(TIXH), 32     ! line 10
TD9B    KF, TCHCNT(TIXF), 40         ! line 11
        BZAH, TD9C                   ! line 12
        LV, TIXG, 0.0(TIXF)          ! line 13
        ST(BU,32), 0.0(TIXF), 32     ! line 14
        SV, TIXG, $R                 ! line 15
TD9C    CBH, TIXF, TD9B              ! line 16
        ST(BU,32), 0.0(TIXH), 32     ! line 17
        CBH, TIXH, TD9A              ! line 18
TD9     LX, TCTWDX, 0.0($15)         ! line 20 -RESTORE THE ENTRY
                                      !           CONTROL WORD
        B, TB1F                      ! line 21

! ---- MULTI UNIT SCAN ----------------------------------------------
TA9D    L, TUNITK(TIXF), 46          ! line 25 -NUMBER OF UNITS TO
                                      !           A CHANNEL
        LC, TIXG, $R                 ! line 26
        BXCZ, TB9                    ! line 27
        LV, TIXG, TUNTBA(TIXF)       ! line 28 -THE UNIT TABLE
                                      !           ADDRESS
TA9E    BB, TCHAVL(TIXF), TA9F       ! line 29 -IF CHANNEL NOT
                                      !           AVAILABLE
        BB, TCHOWN(TIXG), TA9FA      ! line 30 -IF MCP LEVEL IT IS
                                      !           NOT AVAIL TO PP
        BZB, TUNAVL(TIXG), TC9       ! line 31 -IF UNIT IS AVAILABLE
TA9F    BZB, TUNASG(TIXG), TN        ! line 32 -IF THE UNIT IS
                                      !           ASSIGNED
TA9FA   LVI, TX1BR, TA9G             ! line 33 -LOAD FOR SUB ROUTINE
                                      !           BRANCH
        CT0011(BU,2), TUNRES(TIXG)   ! line 34 -IS UNIT RESERVED BY PP
        BZRZ, TC10                   ! line 35 -YES
TA9G    CB+, TIXG, TA9E              ! line 36

! ---- ADVANCE THE UNIT COUNT TABLE FOR ANOTHER CHANNEL -------------
        LF, TCHCNT(TIXH)             ! line 41
        BRZ, TB9                     ! line 42
        SV, TIXF, $R                 ! line 43
        ST, TCHADD(TIXH), 46         ! line 44
        V+I, TIXH, 0.32              ! line 45
        C+I, TIXH, 1.0               ! line 46
        KF, TLUCT                    ! line 47 -LARGEST UNIT COUNT
        BZAH, TB9                    ! line 48
        ST, TLUCT                    ! line 49
        B, TB9                       ! line 50

! ---- ADD TO THE UNIT COUNT IN THE MULTI UNIT TABLE ----------------
TC9     BZB, TEQUIP(TIXF), TA9G      ! line 54 -IF NO EQUIP ON
                                      !           THIS CHANNEL
        M+1, TCHCNT(TIXH)            ! line 55 -ADD ONE TO THE COUNT
        B, TA9G                      ! line 56
        END, TD9A

